	<li>Beverage consumption during lunches &amp; dinner.</li>
	<li>Indian passport holders may enter Uzbekistan visa-free for up to 30 days, provided they meet the eligibility conditions.<br>
	&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Visa-Free Entry Requirements:</strong><br>
	&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;• New Zeeland, UAE residency.<br>
	&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;• Valid multiple-entry visa from one of the following: USA, UK, Schengen countries, Canada, Australia, Japan, South Korea, New Zealand.<br>
	&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;• Valid onward/return ticket.<br>
	&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;• Compliance with other applicable entry requirements.<br>
	&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>If conditions are not met:</strong><br>
	&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;• A visa is required before travel.<br>
	&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;• Indian passport holders can apply for a single-entry e-Visa at USD 30 per person (processing time: 3–5 working days).<br>
	<strong>Note:</strong> The Uzbekistan visa/e-Visa is not included in the package price.</li>
</ol>
